WHO markdown:
范蠡 was the chief strategist and diplomat of 越王勾踐 (Goujian) of Yue, a small state on the southeastern Chinese coast that had just been crushed by Wu and reduced to a rump around Mt. Kuaiji (會稽) in the early 5th century BCE. In 國語·越語下 — a state-speech record compiled within roughly a century of his death — he is the man the king summons year after year and who keeps answering 未可也, "not yet." He framed every situation through three channels he names himself: 持盈者與天、定傾者與人、節事者與地 ("when at the full, accord with Heaven; when in danger, accord with people; when handling affairs, accord with the ground") — 國語/卷21.史記 records that he was made 上將軍 and that he personally negotiated his own release from Wu as a hostage (質) and helped reduce 吴 in 473 BCE — 史記/卷41. After the war he refused Goujian's offer to share the kingdom, saying 「君行令，臣行意」 ("your word is command; mine is intent") and sailed away with his household — 史記/卷41, echoed in 國語/卷21. He then reinvented himself three times: 鴟夷子皮 farming at the sea's edge in Qi, briefly prime minister of Qi, and finally 陶朱公 (Lord Zhu of Tao) at the market-hub of Tao, where 史記 says he died of old age and 太史公 concludes 「范蠡三遷皆有榮名，名垂後世」 ("each of Fan Li's three relocations brought him honoured name"). His commercial method is credited to his teacher 計然 (Ji Ran) — 史記·貨殖列傳 quotes 計然 directly on buying low and selling high, and quotes 范蠡 saying 「計然之策七，越用其五而得意。既已施於國，吾欲用之家」 ("Ji Ran's plan had seven parts; Yue used five and prevailed. Now that it has been applied to the state, I want to apply it to the household") — so the economic doctrine is *his teacher's, executed by him*, not his own invention.

WHO source: runs/20261013-four-seats/identity/fan-li.md

ITEM 1 {
 "n": 1,
 "title": "Keep to the time: Heaven's time and human affairs together",
 "kind": "decision rule",
 "rule": "While Heaven's time has not arisen, do not be the one who attacks; while human affairs have not arisen,\ndo not be the one who starts. Success needs human affairs joined with Heaven and Earth. When one had come and the\nother had not, he told the king to wait.",
 "words": "「夫聖人隨時以行，是謂守時。天時不作，弗為人客；人事不起，弗為之始。」 — \"The sage moves with the\ntime; this is called keeping to the time. When Heaven's time has not arisen, do not be the guest [the attacker];\nwhen human affairs have not arisen, do not be the one who begins.\" / 「人事至矣，天應未也，王姑待之。」 — \"Human\naffairs have arrived; Heaven's response has not. For now, wait.\" / 「天應至矣，人事未盡也，王姑待之。」…\n「夫人事必將與天地相參，然後乃可以成功。」 — \"Heaven's response has arrived; human affairs are not yet at their\nend. For now, wait.\" … \"Human affairs must be joined with Heaven and Earth as a three; only then can success be\nachieved.\" (韋昭: 攻者為客; 先動為始; 人事 = 怨叛、逆亂之萌; 參，三也.)",
 "source": "國語·越語下 (Wikisource 國語/卷21): §范蠡進諫句踐持盈定傾節事 (國語21:3). There he tells the king that\nattacking now 「逆於天而不和於人」; the king attacked and lost (21:5). Also §范蠡謂人事至而天應未至 (21:15), on Wu's\ninternal decay, and §范蠡謂人事與天地相參乃可以成功 (21:19).",
 "label": "quoted",
 "from": "top-12 #1 (split), with top-10 #1's quotes restored",
 "kind_tag": "decision rule"
}

ITEM 2 {
 "n": 2,
 "title": "Three kinds of state affairs, three things to go by",
 "kind": "decision rule",
 "rule": "A state's affairs are keeping what is full, steadying what is tilting, and regulating affairs. Keeping\nthe full goes with Heaven, steadying the tilting goes with people, and regulating affairs goes with Earth. Heaven's\nway, in his words, is full without overflowing, flourishing without arrogance, and labouring without boasting of\nits work.",
 "words": "「夫國家之事，有持盈，有定傾，有節事。」/「持盈者與天，定傾者與人，節事者與地。」/\n「天道盈而不溢，盛而不驕，勞而不矜其功。」 — \"In the affairs of a state there is keeping the full, steadying the\ntilting, and regulating affairs.\" / \"Keeping the full goes with Heaven; steadying the tilting goes with people;\nregulating affairs goes with Earth.\" / \"Heaven's way is full but does not overflow, flourishes but is not arrogant,\nlabours but does not boast of its work.\" (韋昭: 持，守也; 盈，滿也; 傾，危也; 節，制也; 與天，法天也.)",
 "source": "國語21:3. He repeats it after the defeat at 21:7 (「君王其忘之乎？持盈者與天…」) and fills in two of the\nthree: 與人 at 21:7 (→ #15) and 與地 at 21:9 (→ #3). 史記·越王句踐世家 41:18 has the variant\n「持滿者與天，定傾者與人，節事者以地」.",
 "label": "quoted",
 "from": "top-12 #1 (split)",
 "kind_tag": "decision rule"
}
